# Release and deploy
<%#hasCd%>

## Pipeline
1. Merge to `<%defaultBranch%>` after CI is green. `cd.yml` calls `ci.yml` first, then builds each image **once** with an immutable tag `sha-<12 chars>` and pushes it to `ghcr.io/<%ownerLower%>/`.
2. Environments, in order:
<%#environments%>
   - **<%name%>**: trigger `<%trigger%>`, URL <%url%>
<%/environments%>
3. After each deploy the workflow runs the facts against the live URL (`--no-runtime --base-url web=<url>`). A failing fact fails the deploy job: treat the release as bad.
4. Production approval: configure required reviewers on the GitHub Environment (Settings -> Environments).

## Releasing
```bash
git tag v1.2.3 && git push origin v1.2.3        # tags trigger the tag-based environments
# or: Actions -> CD -> Run workflow -> choose the environment
```

## Rollback
Images are immutable, so rollback is "deploy the previous good tag":
```bash
./scripts/deploy.sh <environment> sha-<previous-12-chars>
```
then confirm with `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc facts --no-runtime --base-url web=<url>`.

## Deploy target: `<%cdTarget%>`
Implementation: `scripts/deploy.sh` -> `deploy/targets/<%cdTarget%>.sh`. Required secrets are listed at the top of that script and are set per GitHub Environment, never in the repo.

## Checklist
- [ ] `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc verify` green on the commit being released
- [ ] Contract changes are backward compatible, or clients ship first
- [ ] New env vars and secrets exist in the target environment
- [ ] Post-deploy facts PASS; evidence artifact attached to the run
<%/hasCd%>
